WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.395
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:10.600
SPEAKER: Geospatial
insights can help

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.410
your organization realize a
more prosperous and sustainable

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.290
future.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:16.420
Want to see how?

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.550
Let's take a look at
Google Earth Engine,

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:20.890
a powerful platform
that makes uncovering

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:23.740
these valuable
insights possible.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.290
Earth Engine was launched
over a decade ago

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.630
as a geospatial
analytics platform

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.830
that takes planet scale data--

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.890
and I mean that literally
and figuratively--

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.770
and couples it with
the computing power

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:38.470
of Google's infrastructure.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.260
Researchers, scientists,
and developers

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:44.260
alike have been driving
impact across sectors

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:48.310
by detecting and qualifying
changes, mapping global trends,

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:49.270
and more.

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:52.630
Consider a research team who
used Earth Engine to build

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:55.060
an innovative monitoring
and alerting tool

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:57.820
to protect against
illegal logging.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.550
So how might that
relate to your work?

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:03.190
Let's dig in.

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:06.640
We're excited to now provide
limited commercial availability

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:10.330
of Earth Engine so data and
geospatial professionals,

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:14.050
like you, can accelerate
impact within your own business

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.300
and augment the
impact-driven work being

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:19.360
done every day by the vibrant
community of Earth Engine

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:20.860
users.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:22.390
Here are three
things for you to put

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:25.120
in your mental map for how
Earth Engine can help you

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:26.440
on your team--

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:29.740
the data catalog,
development flexibility,

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:33.370
and common business drivers.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:35.320
First, the data.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.480
Living up to Google's
mission, that

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:39.730
is, to organize the
world's information

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:42.400
and make it more
accessible and useful,

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.920
we've cataloged
over 50 petabytes

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:48.590
of analysis-ready data about
the Earth's present, past,

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:49.970
and future.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:52.330
This includes climate
and weather data,

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:56.020
imagery from satellite platforms
such as Landsat, Sentinel,

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.930
and MODIS, and other
geophysical data,

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:02.860
like terrain and land cover
maps in both raster and vector

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:04.240
formats.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.750
Time series data stretches back
over 40 years in some cases.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.280
And on the other
hand of the clock,

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:14.080
there are many
real-time data sets too.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.750
The increasing volume
of satellite launches

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:19.120
with ever more
sophisticated sensors

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.720
is helping fuel an explosion
of fresh, high frequency Earth

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.740
observation data as well.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:27.880
So that means more and more
data becoming available,

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.710
along with the
need for platforms

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:33.940
to be able to ingest, store,
and process them efficiently.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:36.160
Fortunately, this
is something Google

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.090
and Earth Engine are
equipped to handle at scale.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.860
What that means
is that users like

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.770
you get to focus on
just the fun stuff--

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:48.700
geospatial analytics
and data science.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.320
Accessing the data
in Earth Engine

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.640
is as simple as a
few lines of code.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.380
So bring your hypotheses, know
the extent of your analysis

00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:00.490
and time horizon, and
you're ready to go.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:04.690
Second, consider the flexibility
of the development environment.

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:07.030
Earth Engine has a
computational engine

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:09.940
that can handle the
complexity and global scale

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:13.600
that thousands of PhDs,
developers, and data scientists

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.700
throw at it every day.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:18.400
There are several options
for you to access and work

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.920
with the data that takes
advantage of that computing

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.180
power.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.280
You can connect to the
Earth Engine service

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:26.650
through one of its APIs.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:29.350
Client libraries for
JavaScript and Python

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:32.110
translate complex
geospatial analyses

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:34.630
into Earth Engine requests.

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:36.940
Or connect directly to
Earth Engine servers

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.980
using the REST API.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:41.980
Earth Engine also provides
an interactive environment

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:45.280
with an online code editor,
ideal for prototyping

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.470
and iteration.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:49.210
More comfortable in Python?

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:53.260
Earth Engine also works in
Python notebooks like Colab.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:55.300
You can even run
inference directly

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.850
from satellite
images using Cloud AI

00:03:57.850 --> 00:03:59.950
Platform from Earth Engine.

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:01.600
And the results
are returned to you

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.540
as an image or set of features
right in Earth Engine.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:06.040
That's cool, right?

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.150
When you're ready
to go global scale,

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:10.390
you can take advantage of
Earth Engine's batch mode

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:13.720
to process petabytes of data
within a massively parallelized

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:16.839
environment with zero
configuration or server

00:04:16.839 --> 00:04:18.190
management.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:21.160
To create interactive
experiences of your analyses

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.530
that can be securely
shared with your users,

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:26.500
you can use Earth Engine
apps with its library of UI

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:30.380
components and hosted platform.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:33.580
Finally, there are a handful
of common business drivers

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.250
that you or maybe someone
else in your organization

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:39.000
are thinking about already.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.610
Vexing questions,
like how resilient

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:44.580
is my business to effects
from climate change?

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:47.340
How or is my
business compounding

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:50.520
economic and societal
issues around deforestation

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:52.200
or pollution?

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:57.480
Or what else can I do to support
our ESG reporting initiatives?

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:01.260
There are common themes we see
across commercial applications.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.630
One, for example, is
using climate data

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:06.630
to understand risk or
impacts to physical assets

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:09.300
like infrastructure or
real estate holdings

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:12.210
across disparate geographies.

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:15.090
Beyond assessing risk, there
are many other use cases

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:18.420
to spark your creativity too.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:21.120
OK, we've covered a
lot about Earth Engine,

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.880
and there's so much more
for you to check out.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.580
Head on over to our website
where you can explore the data

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.940
catalog, read through a few
case studies as inspiration,

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:32.070
and register your
team's interest

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:34.950
in accessing Earth
Engine during preview.

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:37.950
We can't wait to hear about
the initiatives you all

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:40.950
will be driving, and the
combined impact we can make

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:44.280
together with Google Earth
Engine for creating prosperity,

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:48.840
resilience, and sustainability
for your organization.

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:53.090
